The invariant ⬤○○⬤⬤⬤⬤○⬤⬤⬤⬤⬤ lacuna is a stemma problem. All extant Kunoichi no Jutsu witnesses show the same black/white ordering in the same position, so the explanation has to be a single normalising event in the archetype that is then copied faithfully.

A, B, D, E, F, G and even H can all be modelled as one-origin-to-many-copies mechanisms that stay inside documented Tokugawa manuscript culture:

* A authorial/institutional self-censorship before presentation to the Shogun;
* B social/moral censorship by copyists re women’s roles and modesty;
* D Oniwaban state-secret redaction;
* E aburidashi heat-reveal invisible ink transcribed as blanks by a non-initiate scribe;
* F a kuden/oral mnemonic colour-symbol code mis-copied as a schematic placeholder;
* G a single damaged archetype whose conventional scribal placeholder is reproduced downstream;
* H a normalising misreading of a real Edo esoteric set such as Kuji-in/kujiho into schematic placeholders.

All are speculative in detail but historically intelligible in kind.

C cannot be rendered that way without inventing history. The Bansenshukai was compiled c.1676 by Fujibayashi Nagatake/Nagatane/Masatake and presented to the Shogunate in the 1670s. Hattori Hanzō/Masanari is Sengoku-early Edo, d.1596/c.1627, decades before compilation. The Saigō house attested in shogunal politics is Satsuma Saigō, late Edo/Meiji, e.g. Saigō Takamori, ~200 years later. There is no Tokugawa-era Lady Saigō, no documented Hattori stepdaughter who was a key shogunal figure, and no archival link placing a court lady’s kunoichi use at the centre of Tokugawa legitimacy in the 1670s.

Even de-personalised, the mechanism is impossible: a private individual would have to locate and uniformly redact the Kunoichi no Jutsu block in every independent samurai/temple copying line after 1676 and leave the identical black/white circle placeholder in all witnesses in order to protect Tokugawa lineage/Pax Tokugawa from a shinobi career that by definition postdates the alleged actor. That is a fabricated prosopography, an anachronistic trans-century kinship and chronology, and no plausible agent or pan-tradition control for a uniform lacuna.

H is doctrinally syncretic and unsupported — chakras, “nine holes of the female body”, Taoist erotic alchemy — but it does not violate known chronology or prosopography and can be read as a one-origin symbolic misreading of real Bansenshukai esoteric material that is then copied. C requires a person and a timeline that demonstrably could not exist and an impossible mode of uniform redaction. That makes it the least plausible of the set.

