Round 4 public votes: 1,10,11,12,15,2,3,4,5,6,8,9 vote C as least plausible; 13,14,7 hold H. Majority has converged on C over three rounds.

Core pro-C arguments that persist:
Bansenshukai compiled c.1676 by Fujibayashi Nagatake/Nagatane/Masatake/Yasuta/Masatake and presented in 1670s. Hattori Hanzō/Masanari d.1596/c.1627, decades before compilation. Saigō house attested in shogunal politics is Satsuma Saigō, late Edo/Meiji e.g. Saigō Takamori ~200 years later. No Tokugawa-era Lady Saigō, no documented Hattori stepdaughter, no archival link to a kunoichi political crisis threatening Tokugawa legitimacy in the 1670s.
